---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="MathLoop Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for MathLoop by Kroma Digital.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">App Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for MathLoop</h1>
      <p>Privacy information for the MathLoop Android application.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated: September 7, 2026</strong></p>

      <h2>1. About MathLoop</h2>
      <p>MathLoop is an educational Android application designed to help children practice basic mathematics through short daily learning activities.</p>
      <p>MathLoop is developed and maintained by Kroma Digital.</p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use MathLoop, including information that may be processed by third-party services used by the app.</p>

      <h2>2. Account Registration</h2>
      <p>MathLoop does not require users to create an account or provide a name, email address, phone number, or other account information to use the app.</p>

      <h2>3. Learning Data and App Settings</h2>
      <p>MathLoop stores learning progress, preferences, and other app settings locally on the user's device.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not operate a server for collecting or storing this learning data.</p>
      <p>Deleting the app or clearing its application data may remove locally stored progress and settings.</p>

      <h2>4. Advertising</h2>
      <p>MathLoop displays banner advertisements using Google AdMob and the Google Mobile Ads SDK.</p>
      <p>Because MathLoop is intended for children, advertising is configured to comply with applicable Google Play Families requirements. Personalized advertising, interest-based advertising, and remarketing are not intended to be used for children.</p>
      <p>Google and its advertising services may process certain technical information as necessary to provide, secure, measure, and improve advertising services.</p>
      <p>Depending on the Google Mobile Ads SDK configuration and applicable platform requirements, this information may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate general location;</li>
        <li>information about interactions with the app or advertisements;</li>
        <li>diagnostic and performance information, such as crash or app performance data;</li>
        <li>device or app identifiers, where permitted and applicable; and</li>
        <li>other technical information required to provide and protect the advertising service.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not use MathLoop to ask children to provide personal information for advertising purposes.</p>
      <p>For more information about how Google handles information, please review Google's privacy policies and information about Google services.</p>

      <h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>MathLoop is designed for educational use by children.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not intentionally ask children to provide personal information such as their name, email address, phone number, precise location, photographs, contacts, or account credentials in order to use MathLoop.</p>
      <p>Advertising and third-party services used in the app are intended to be configured in accordance with applicable child-directed requirements, including relevant Google Play Families policies.</p>
      <p>Where required, advertising requests are treated as child-directed and personalized advertising is disabled.</p>
      <p>Parents and guardians are encouraged to review the app and its Google Play listing before allowing a child to use it.</p>

      <h2>6. Google Play Billing</h2>
      <p>MathLoop may offer purchases through Google Play, such as purchasing an option to remove advertising.</p>
      <p>Payments are processed by Google Play.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not receive or store users' full credit-card or other payment-card details. Payment information is handled by Google according to Google's own terms and privacy practices.</p>
      <p>Kroma Digital may receive limited transaction-related information necessary to determine whether a purchase has been completed and to provide the purchased functionality.</p>

      <h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>MathLoop may use services provided by Google, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Play services;</li>
        <li>Google Play Billing;</li>
        <li>Google AdMob; and</li>
        <li>Google Mobile Ads SDK.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These services may process information according to their own privacy policies and applicable settings.</p>
      <p>Google's Privacy Policy is available at:</p>
      <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></p>
      <p>Information about how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services is available at:</p>
      <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></p>

      <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital does not sell children's personal information.</p>
      <p>MathLoop does not require users to submit personal information directly to Kroma Digital in order to use the app.</p>
      <p>Technical information may be processed by Google or other service providers used by the app where necessary to provide platform, advertising, billing, security, diagnostic, or related functionality, subject to their respective privacy practices and the configuration of those services.</p>

      <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>Learning progress and app settings stored locally by MathLoop remain on the user's device until they are deleted by the user, removed through application data controls, or removed when the app is uninstalled, depending on the Android device and operating system behavior.</p>
      <p>Information processed independently by Google or other platform services is subject to the retention practices of those service providers.</p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>Kroma Digital takes reasonable measures to minimize unnecessary collection of information and to limit the app's use of personal information.</p>
      <p>However, no electronic system, device, or network transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated if MathLoop's features, advertising, SDKs, billing, storage, data practices, or applicable legal and platform requirements change.</p>
      <p>Any updated version will be published on this page with a revised "Last updated" date.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>If you are a parent, guardian, or other user and have questions about this Privacy Policy or MathLoop's privacy practices, please contact Kroma Digital through the Kroma Digital Contact page:</p>
      <p><a href="/contact">https://kroma-digital.pages.dev/contact</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
